sed "s/^X//" >README2 <<'END_OF_README2'
XMAHJONGG Version 1.1
X
XCopyright 1988 Mark A. Holm
X
XPermission is given to copy and distribute for non-profit purposes.
X
XThis game will operate on any Sun hardware that I know of with either
Xa monochrome or a color bit mapped tube running Sun 3.2 UNIX or later.
XMost of the development was done on a Sun 100U running Sun 3.5.
X
XPlease Note!! The automagic screen type determination will not recognize
Xall screen types unless compiled with <sys/fbio.h> from a 3.5 OS. If
Xcompiled with 3.2 not all monochrome types are recognized. Also note that I did
Xnot have enough time or alternate screen types to checkl out the 386.
X
XTHIS IS A PATCH KIT (Patch 1 and 2)
XINSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:
X
X1. 	cd to source from parts 1-4 and move icons.c.Z.uue[12] to
X	icons.c.Z.uue[12].680x0.
X
X2.	Unpack these kits in the same directory and run the file 
X	mahjongg.patch1 through patch. Edit the Makefile to
X	set MANLOC and DESTDIR to the appropriate locations.
X
X4.	Move the appropriate icons.o.Z.uue[12].{680x0 or 386} to
X	icons.o.Z.uue[12] for your target machine.
X
X3.	run 'make install'.  
X
XI have distributed the tiles as uuencoded-compressed .o files to
Xsave on file sizes and to preserve the "Look and feel" of the game.
XIf you would like the source to the icons and the patches to iconedit
Xso you can modify them send a request (and possibly a small
Xdonation ;^) to the address below.
X
XIf you have any questions or problems/bug reports, send them to me:
X
XMark A. Holm
Xtektronix!tessi!exc!markh
END_OF_README2
